WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.952
Data quality has multiple dimensions.

00:00:02.952 --> 00:00:05.837
Completeness is not the same as validity.

00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:08.192
Validity is not the same as uniqueness.

00:00:08.192 --> 00:00:10.982
Timeliness asks a different question again.

00:00:10.982 --> 00:00:14.452
Measure these dimensions separately whenever possible.

00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:21.537
A single score can be useful for triage, but it can hide which problem actually caused the low score.

00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:26.192
Validation is rule-based detection, not automatic correction.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:32.817
A failed email-shape check tells you that a record deserves attention; it does not tell you the correct email.

00:00:32.817 --> 00:00:39.401
Treat quality flags as evidence that can drive quarantine, review, or a documented repair process.
